    {
      "id": "claim_ecc9ec98b14344b6ba8f3d3b0e9611b7",
      "statement": "The server-owned runtime (agent graph, composite backend, and offload operation) is built and cached exactly once per process; caching is load-bearing because MCP discovery, sandbox creation, and atexit cleanup registration must each happen exactly once, and building per request would re-discover MCP servers, leak sandbox sessions, and stack duplicate atexit handlers.",
